{"id": "176606", "revid": "162256", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=176606", "title": "Smilavi\u010dy", "text": "Smilavi\u010dy (Belarusian: \"\u0421\u043c\u0456\u043b\u0430\u0432\u0456\u0447\u044b\"; also commonly known as Smilovichi, a transliteration of the Russian: \"\u0421\u043c\u0438\u043b\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0438\") is a town of 5,000 people (2017) in Minsk voblas\u0107.\nUnderstand.\nSmilavi\u010dy is best known for being the birthplace of painters Cha\u00efm Soutine and Schraga Zarfin.\nApart from Belarusians, Jews and Tatars traditionally lived in Smilovichi. Most Jews died during World War II or moved to other places, including the United States and Israel.\nTatars settled in Smilovichi more than 600 years ago. The first known mosque in the town operated in the 1880s. In 1930 it was destroyed. The modern Tatar community in Smilovichi has more than a hundred families. \nIn the post-war period, people from Bashkortostan also live in Smilovichi due to the construction of the felt and felt industry.\nGet in.\nIt is on the Minsk - Mogilev highway 27 km east of Minsk, 30 km west of Cherven, and 21 km from Rudensk railway station."}
{"id": "176613", "revid": "771685", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=176613", "title": "Pest County", "text": "Pest (Hungarian: /pe\u0283t/) county is in Central Hungary. It surrounds the national capital Budapest, but does not include it. About 2/3 of the county's population of 1.3 million (2018) live in the suburbs of Budapest.\nCities.\nEastern part.\n\"Dunakeszi, V\u00e1c, Szentendre, Pom\u00e1z, Pilisv\u00f6r\u00f6sv\u00e1r, Nagymaros, Ver\u0151ce, Szob and Visegr\u00e1d are described in the Danube Bend article.\"\nOther destinations.\nIts Catholic church was built in the 1830s. In its garden there is an obelisk commemorating Prince R\u00e1k\u00f3czi."}
{"id": "176617", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=176617", "title": "Danube Bend", "text": "Danube Bend (Hungarian: \"Dunakanyar\") is a curve of the Danube in Hungary and gives its name to this entire region.\nGet around.\nFerries of Danube river.\nThere are many ferries across the Danube River, including V\u00e1c\u2014Tahit\u00f3tfalu, Szob\u2014Pilismar\u00f3t, Fels\u0151g\u00f6d\u2014Sur\u00e1ny, Als\u00f3g\u00f6d\u2014Szigetmonostor, P\u00f3csmegyer\u2014Le\u00e1nyfalu, Dunakeszi\u2014Hor\u00e1ny, Kisoroszi\u2014Visegr\u00e1d/Szentgy\u00f6rgypuszta, Visegr\u00e1d\u2014Nagymaros, and Pilismar\u00f3t\u2014Zebeg\u00e9ny."}
